# ============================================================================
# FlowAblation / 1D ablation ONSET  (Hydro2, ablation.on = 1, ablation.conduction = 1)
#
# The surface starts BELOW the ablation temperature and reaches it later: the transition between the
# two regimes of the capped wall temperature (Ablation.H).  A solid slab 0 < x < L = 0.1 with an
# adiabatic back (x = 0) is brought into contact at t = 0 with gas at rest at T_g = 1 filling
# 0.1 < x < 0.5 (adiabatic end).  Gas of input_1D_Stefan2 (k_g 4.861e-3, alpha_g 1.389e-3,
# e_g = sqrt(k rho c) = 0.1304); solid rho_s 1, cp_s 0.875, k_s = 4 k_g -> e_s = e_g (sig = 1) and
# alpha_s = 16 alpha_g, so the slab heats through quickly.  T_s0 = 0.99, T_abl = 0.9975, Q* = 0.01.
#   stage 1 (no recession): contact temperature T_i = 0.995, then the slab heats up and the surface
#     temperature rises,  T_w = T_s0 + (T_g - T_s0)/2 [1 + erfc(L/sqrt(alpha_s t))]   (sig = 1, gas
#     semi-infinite; Laplace transform / images), and reaches T_abl at
#     t_abl = L^2 / (alpha_s [erfc^-1(2 (T_abl - T_i)/(T_g - T_s0))]^2) = 1.97830
#   stage 2 (T_w = T_abl): rho_s Q* ds/dt = q_g - q_s; no closed form -> fine-grid front-fixing reference
#     (reference/ablation_onset_reference.py, verified against the closed form above and against the
#     two-phase Stefan similarity solution; second-order convergent): s(t = 6) = 0.024085.
# Constant properties, gas at rest (1 % temperature difference), no blowing, as in input_1D_Stefan2.
# Measured (2026-10-29, square cells, t = 6; reference/Images/R32_Onset):
#   cells   onset t_abl          recession s(6)      gas profile (% of dT)
#   100     1.98431 (+0.30 %)    0.023829 (-1.07 %)  0.087
#   200     1.98282 (+0.23 %)    0.023906 (-0.75 %)  0.081
#   400     1.98124 (+0.15 %)    0.023972 (-0.47 %)  0.070
#   no recession before onset (|s| < 1e-13); solid profile error < 1e-3 %.  The residual surface-temperature
#   deviation before onset (<= 0.5 % of dT, at t ~ 0.7) follows the gas pressure (correlation 0.98): acoustic
#   waves from the initial contact, reflected between the wall and x = 0.5; the reference has no acoustics.
#
# Run (from bin/), square cells (cost ~ N^3, diffusive dt ~ dx^2: 100 cells 98 s, 200 cells 570 s on 1 core, 400 cells 43 min on 2):
#   mpirun --bind-to none -np 1 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowAblation/input_1D_AblationOnset plot_file=<dir>/output
#       (200 cells; for N cells add  amr.n_cell="N 4" geometry.prob_hi="0.5 2/N 0.0"  [and amr.max_grid_size=200 with -np 2])
# Check:  python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/ablation_onset_check.py <dir> [<dir2> ...]
# Reference self-test:  python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/ablation_onset_reference.py verify
# ============================================================================
